{"repositoryId":432762574,"availability":"available","full":"KittyMac/Sextant","name":"Sextant","description":"High performance JSONPath queries for Swift","category":"Other","language":"Swift","stars":68,"forks":10,"created":"2021-11-28T16:19:33Z","updated":"2026-07-28T14:10:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://www.swift-linux.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.546Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.546Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.546Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.546Z","stars":68,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sextant is a complete, high performance JSONPath implementation written in Swift. It was originally ported from SMJJSONPath, which in turn is a tight adaptation of the Jayway JsonPath implementation. Sextant has since been updated to bring it into compliance with other JSON path implementations (see issue), so this specific implementation now varies from the SMJJSONPath/Jayway implementation.","The original Stefan Goessner JsonPath implemenentation was released in 2007, and from it spawned dozens of different implementations. This JSONPath Comparison chart shows the wide array of available implemenations, and at the time of this writing a Swift implementation is not present (note that there exists the SwiftPath project, but it is not included in said chart due to critical errors when running on Linux.","The rest of this section is largely adapted from the Jayway JsonPath Getting Started section."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/KittyMac/Sextant/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bdd57d64886f8f3bd164586930ae7c230fc05fe33e38a2782fd4dcd20af01492","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.679Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:21:56.679Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Sextant is a complete, high performance JSONPath implementation written in Swift. It was originall